SOURCE: EU AI Act | Article 5
TITLE: Exceptions to prohibited AI practices

By way of derogation from Article 3(d), the use of real-time remote biometric identification systems may be permitted in the following cases:
(a) for targeted search of identified victims of crime;
(b) for prevention of imminent threats to the safety of persons;
(c) for identification of persons convicted of serious crimes;
(d) for interests of national security, in accordance with Union and Member State law.
